# A releaser that resolves to nothing is refused under every word that names
# one (panel 176's items 1, 2 and 4), and the note says which word it was
# written under: until 2026-09-25 it said `acquires` under `transfers` and
# `retains` too, and offered `borrows` to a transfer, which is not a repair a
# transfer can take. `--brief` prints the message only, so what this golden
# pins is the code at each position; the note's words are the module's own
# test. `h_wrap` keeps `keep` beside the transfer so the transfer has a
# receiver and only the name is wrong.
extern "unread-releaser-names-its-word.h"
    record H tag hh
    function h_open() -> H acquires h_close
    function h_close(x: H consumes)
    function h_wrap(x: H transfers nothere, keep: H)  #~ unread_releaser
    function h_ref(x: H retains nothere)  #~ unread_releaser
    function h_get(x: H) -> H retains nothere  #~ unread_releaser

function main()
    a = h_open()
    h_close(x: a)
